# No gradient card top borders

Joe does **not** want the "AI border" treatment on boxes: colored or rainbow gradient strips along the top edge of cards, panels, or containers (typically a 2–3px `::before` pseudo-element with `var(--spectrum)` or phase-tint gradients).

## Avoid

- `::before` / `::after` top accent bars on cards (`.card::before { height: 3px; background: linear-gradient(...) }`)
- Phase-colored top borders on grid items, step cards, model cards, or similar UI boxes
- Any decorative "spectrum rim" on container edges meant to signal AI/tech

## Prefer instead

- Uniform `border: 1px solid var(--glass-border)` or `--site-line`
- Subtle background elevation (`rgba(255,255,255,0.03)` on dark, white + shadow on light sections)
- Typography accents (kickers, headings) for color — not box rims
- Small neutral bullet markers or icons inside the card if emphasis is needed

Gradient **text** (`.cin-spectrum`, headline highlights) is fine when requested. The objection is specifically **gradient borders on boxes**.

When redesigning cards, never reintroduce top gradient borders unless the user explicitly asks for them.
